# VeritasVault.net Landing Page - Windsurf Rules

## Project Overview
Next.js 15 app with TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Supabase auth, and dual theme system (Corporate/Standard)

## Build Commands
- `pnpm dev` - Development server
- `pnpm build` - Production build
- `pnpm lint` - ESLint check
- `pnpm dup-check` - Check duplicate code

## Code Standards
- Use TypeScript strict mode with `@/*` path aliases
- Functional components with proper TypeScript typing
- Tailwind CSS with CSS variables for theming
- Radix UI components for primitives
- camelCase variables/functions, PascalCase components
- External → internal → relative import order

## Architecture
- `/app` - Next.js App Router pages
- `/components` - Reusable UI components  
- `/lib` - Utilities, services, auth helpers
- Supabase for auth/data, NextAuth.js integration
- AI services: OpenAI, DeepInfra, Groq, Fal.ai

## Important
- ESLint/TypeScript errors ignored in builds
- Keep all rules files (.windsurfrules, .cursorrules, CLAUDE.md, .github/copilot-instructions.md) in sync
